aims-os-outils (2.1+1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New package: the AIMS Senegal lab software on a personal computer, for
    students who want on their own laptop what they use in the lab.
    aims-os-centre-senegal-labo cannot go there: its postinst locks every
    local sudo account and it opens IT remote access. aims-os-outils depends
    on every AIMS OS layer and on the Debian packages the lab profile adds,
    and its service aims-outils fetches the latest published lab package,
    takes only the installer (aims-labo-extras), the weekly update
    (aims-labo-update) and their helpers (Zoom without Vulkan, separate
    Anaconda font cache, Packet Tracer fix, JupyterLab launchers, aims-vm,
    aims-db, aims-acrobat), then runs them.
  * The first pass starts from the postinst without blocking apt (its apt
    commands wait for the dpkg lock) and is resumed the next day by a daily
    timer until it completes; afterwards the timer runs the weekly update.
    A pass that gets cut short is retried the next day instead of the next
    week, the gap seen on lab machines switched off mid-update.
  * Nothing is downloaded on a metered connection (mobile data, phone
    hotspot). Packet Tracer and the virtual machine images, served by the
    campus server, are installed once the computer reaches it.
  * Conflicts with aims-os-centre-senegal-labo; removing the package removes
    the files taken from it, the Zoom diversion and the font cache settings.

 -- AIMS Senegal IT <hakim@aims-senegal.org>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:30:02 +0000
